<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mir Fateh Ali Khan Talpur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1801</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mir Fateh Ali Khan Talpur was the founder of Talpur rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a>. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baloch">Baloch</a> chief whose family had served the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalhora-dynasty">Kalhora dynasty</a>, he defeated the last Kalhora ruler at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-halani">Battle of Halani</a> in 1783 and was recognised as ruler of Sindh by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durrani-empire">Durrani Empire</a>. He shared power with his brothers from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyderabad-sindh">Hyderabad</a>, beginning the collective rule of the Talpur mirs that lasted until 1843.</p></div>
